      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Toronto Blue Jays' July 4th doubleheader in Seattle was a tale of two extremes, leaving fans bewildered and the standings precarious. <strong>Jays beat Mariners 2-0</strong> in the series opener thanks to Dylan Cease's seven scoreless innings, but the finale collapsed into an <strong>11-0 boat race</strong> fueled by Randy Arozarena's grand slam and three Mariners home runs. Now sitting at 42-47 and third in the AL East, the Jays are 11.5 games behind the division leader, their one-game win streak a fragile reprieve from the 0-11 disaster. Vladimir Guerrero Jr. remains the engine, though he's turned down an All-Star invite, while Cease and Varland head to the game. <strong>Tonight at 5:00 PM ET, the Jays face the Mariners again in a desperate bid to salvage the series and climb back above.500.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 5, 2026"
      },
