        "label": "What's Going On With the Raptors",
        "body": "The Toronto Raptors are no longer chasing wins but building a foundation, closing a season that ended at 46-36 with a 3rd-place Atlantic Division finish to now reshape the roster. <strong>Jaden Bradley, the 50th overall pick from Arizona and Big 12 Player of the Year, has signed a two-way contract</strong>, joining Chucky Hepburn to fill two of the team's limited two-way spots as the front office evaluates size and potential before Summer League. Bradley's resume - 13.3 points, 3.3 rebounds, and 4.4 assists last season - signals a guard who can defend and create, a sharp contrast to the team's recent perimeter struggles. With Garrett Temple moving to Dallas as an assistant and Scottie Barnes' future still unfolding, the focus is now on youth development and cap flexibility. <strong>What to watch this month: how Bradley and Hepburn perform in Summer League, and whether the final two-way spot goes to a big man or a standout undrafted prospect</strong>.",
